[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_core_impl_pretense.py: Resolve all three contract deviations. (1) SemverCoreImplPseudoStateMachine now overrides the Version-owned format and is_prerelease transitions against a bound Version value object (sut(Version) + call_target) with canonical-format and prerelease postcondition asserts, so the fuzz prototype no longer dispatches to the VersionEngine receiver; the real suite binds a Version instance (singletons + as_checked) and exercises format/is_prerelease through the checked proxy. (2) All parse inputs in the real suite now come from the modeled parse domain (PARSED_VERSIONS/VERSION_TEXTS); 1.2.0 replaced by the in-domain 1.2.3, and the parse override asserts the observed Version equals the modeled record. (3) The precedence model is reconciled with the contracted SemVer 2.0.0 ordering: a _precedence_sign oracle (numeric components, numeric-below-string prerelease identifiers, longer prerelease sequences above shared prefixes, build metadata ignored) is now asserted against the engine result on every checked comparison, and the deterministic suite asserts only model-representable relations (numeric ordering, equality of identical versions, prerelease ranked below its normal release in the direction the model represents), removing the alpha.1 > alpha and build-metadata equality assertions that the numerically-only model cannot represent.
