[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/lib/semver_range_impl.py: The empty-clause guard at lines 208-212 is structurally unreachable under the low/semver_range.pyi and low/semver_range_impl.pyi contracts, so it cannot be covered by any conforming scenario. Every call reaches clause compilation only after the union-clause split has already stripped the clause and raised InvalidRangeError when that clause is empty, so a non-empty stripped clause always yields at least one non-whitespace comparator token and the empty-atoms branch is never taken; the contracted empty-union-clause precondition remains fully verified by the earlier union validation. Prune this dead branch, mark it with 'from pretense import unreachable; unreachable()', or annotate it with a coverage exclusion carrying the assumption that empty clauses are rejected before clause compilation.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_core_impl_pretense.py: One contracted precedence case remains unexercised after the latest additions: per low/semver_core.pyi and low/semver_core_impl.pyi, prerelease identifiers that are both numeric MUST compare numerically, which includes the equality result yielding zero precedence, so two versions whose numeric prerelease sequences agree MUST compare as equal. The current scenarios assert numeric ordering only between distinct numeric identifiers (such as 1 lower than 2 and 9 lower than 10) and assert equality only for versions carrying string identifiers or identical plain-release components, so the equal-numeric comparison outcome is never verified. Add a fixed scenario that compares versions sharing equal numeric prerelease identifiers, including identical versions that carry numeric identifiers and numeric identifiers that follow a shared string prefix, asserting zero precedence in both argument orders so the numeric-equality result of the contracted comparison is covered.
