[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_range_impl_pretense.py: Expand deterministic RangeEngine coverage to the full contracted grammar and both True/False outcomes. Added checked scenarios for basic comparators on full versions with both boundary outcomes (exact 1.0.0/1.2.3 equality, <=2.0.0 at-most incl. failing 2.1.0/10.20.30, <2.0.0, >1.0.0 incl. failing 1.0.0/0.0.0, tilde ~1.2.3 on a full version) and for wildcard comparator/caret/tilde forms (>=1.x, ^1.x, 1.2.x, ~1.2.x, !=1.x, >=*, and the whitespace-conjoined >=1.0.0 <2.0.0). Added raw-engine scenarios for forms outside the modeled argument domain: =/== 1.0.0 equality, !=1.0.0 inequality, operator-whitespace '>= 1.0.0', wildcard comparators >1.*, <1.x, <=1.x, caret on major and minor wildcards (^1.x, ^1.2.x), caret full versions including zero-major (^0.1.0) and all-zero (^0.0.0), and a hyphen range with a full semantic upper bound (1.0.0 - 2.3.4), each asserting the matching and non-matching candidates. Added the terminal contract violation scenarios for every contracted InvalidRangeError precondition (empty/whitespace text, comma-delimited comparators, empty union clause, comparator lacking a version, malformed hyphen, bare partial versions and bare-partial comparators, caret on a bare partial, hyphen over bare partials, too many components, numeric component after a wildcard, non-numeric component, leading-zero component) asserting InvalidRangeError with raw_range populated and the engine still usable afterwards.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_core_impl_pretense.py: Add the numeric-prerelease-equality precedence scenario (test_prerelease_numeric_equality): versions sharing equal numeric prerelease identifiers after a shared string prefix compare as zero precedence in both argument orders and for self-comparison, including two distinct Version instances with the same ('alpha','7') numeric sequence and a variant that differs only in build metadata (numeric identifiers compare by value and build metadata is ignored, so all yield zero), plus a checked in-domain comparison of the numeric-identifier version (1.2.3-alpha.7+build.11) against itself asserting zero precedence through the checked transition.
