[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/lib/semver_range_impl.py: parse_range violates the InvalidRangeError contract in low/semver_range.pyi, which defines raw_range as the original malformed range expression string, whereas parse_range (lines 301-320) trims and re-joins the caller text through _normalize_range_text (lines 228-230) and passes that normalized text into _compile (lines 233-254), whose union-clause and comparator error sites copy the normalized text into raw_range. Malformed expressions whose whitespace is changed by normalization therefore raise InvalidRangeError carrying the normalized text instead of the original input: for example an input like '1.x ||' has no trailing whitespace but normalization appends it, and an input ending in '- ' loses its trailing space, so raw_range no longer equals the caller-supplied expression. Trimming is contracted only for the raw_text stored on a successfully parsed VersionRange, never for the error attribute. The latest change only pruned an unreachable guard inside the clause compiler and left this normalization-before-error-reporting defect untouched, so the error path must preserve the original caller-supplied expression while any trimming remains confined to the successful raw_text result.
