[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_range_impl_pretense.py: The expanded suite still leaves specific contracted grammar cases unexercised under low/semver_range.pyi and low/semver_range_impl.pyi. Caret ranges applied to wildcard expressions whose leading numeric component is zero must expand at the first non-zero component, but only caret wildcards with a non-zero major are covered: caret wildcard with zero major and no minor component, caret wildcard with zero major and non-zero minor, and caret wildcard with zero major and zero minor are all absent, so the zero-major fallback expansions are never verified. Caret on a full version likewise still lacks the zero-major, zero-minor, non-zero-patch form in addition to the already covered non-zero-minor and all-zero forms. Tilde ranges applied to a single-component major wildcard are required alongside full-version and multi-component wildcard tilde forms but are never exercised. Finally, the malformed hyphen coverage only reaches expressions whose hyphen-connected bounds are bare partial versions, which raise while parsing the bounds; the contracted InvalidRangeError for a clause that contains a hyphen separator yet does not connect exactly two bounds is never reached, so that error path remains unverified.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_range_impl_pretense.py: Cover the remaining contracted grammar cases in the raw RangeEngine scenarios: caret wildcards whose leading numeric component is zero (^0.x with no minor component, ^0.2.x with a non-zero minor, ^0.0.x with zero major and minor) exercising the first-non-zero-component fallback expansions with matching and non-matching candidates, caret on the zero-major/zero-minor/non-zero-patch full version (^0.0.1 vs 0.0.1 and 0.0.2), and tilde on a single-component major wildcard (~1.x vs 1.5.0 and 2.0.0). Extended the InvalidRangeError fixtures with clauses that contain a hyphen separator yet do not connect exactly two bounds (three-bound '1.0.0 - 2.0.0 - 3.0.0' and lower-bound-less '- 2.0.0'), asserting the terminal contract violation with raw_range populated.
